WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.562 --> 00:00:02.520
KATE BACHELDER ODELL:
I'm Kate Batchelder Odell

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.580
I graduated from Hillsdale
in the class of 2013.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.080
And I'm an editorial writer
for The Wall Street Journal.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.120
I spent a summer studying Latin
in England in high school.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.900
And I was writing my dad these
emails about what was going on

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.930
and what I was up to.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.200
And he wrote back,
you could be a writer.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.633
And what you should do to be a
writer is to read and to write.

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:24.300
So it was just this
natural progression.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.150
It was never this aha
moment, if that makes sense.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.680
And Hillsdale was
just a good fit

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.740
for kind of lining up that
natural interest and curiosity

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.810
with some concrete opportunities
to write for the paper

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.800
but also do a lot of
writing in coursework.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.020
I was the opinions
editor of The Collegian,

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.920
which was a lot of fun.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.595
It was a very good education
in how to work at a newspaper.

00:00:46.595 --> 00:00:47.970
Meeting my husband
at Hillsdale's

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.740
been one of my favorite
things about my experience,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.270
because it's so
much a foundation

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.850
of the life we share.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.130
Hillsdale is also an
education and learning

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.810
how to live with
others, because it

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.030
is being shipwrecked
in rural Michigan

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.650
with 1,400 other people.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.650
Really lean into those
relationships and friendships

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.500
that are every bit as formative
and educational as some

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.732
of the more formal coursework.

00:01:10.732 --> 00:01:13.350
I think people think
opinion writing is

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.800
telling people what you
think about various subjects.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.770
The style of opinion writing
that we do at The Journal

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:25.417
is to report the news and put
it in a analytical narrative.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:26.250
It's an institution.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.010
It's more than 125 years
old, the editorial page is.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.740
In a sense, you are a
steward of something

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.440
that will continue on long after
you're done working for it.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.510
And so it's taking
care of something.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.550
It was really an
exciting, wonderful honor

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.360
to get this award, especially
since so much of my life

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.348
I feel I owe to Hillsdale.

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:49.640
Almost silly to be receiving
an award from somebody who

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.420
gave you everything you have.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.680
I'm honored but also just
amazed and kind of covered

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.910
in gratitude with it all.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

